  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-1",
      "quote": "In the previous sections, we learned about **Tensors** (the data containers) and **Activation Functions** (the decision gates).",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-2",
      "quote": "Now, we combine them into a **Model**.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-3",
      "quote": "A Model is essentially a complex function with “knobs” called **Weights**.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-4",
      "quote": "Training is the process where an **Optimizer** (like Adam) automatically turns these knobs to minimize the **Loss** (the error).",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-5",
      "quote": "Here, you can see how a small network tries to learn a pattern.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-6",
      "quote": "* **The Decision Boundary**: Shows the “map” of what the AI thinks.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-7",
      "quote": "Red areas represent one classification, blue the other.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-8",
      "quote": "* **Weights (Live)**: These are the actual numerical values inside the first layer of the network.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-9",
      "quote": "* **Weight Patterns**: These heatmaps show the numerical values inside each layer's weights, updating live as the optimizer turns the knobs.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    },
    {
      "id": "traininglab-stmt-10",
      "quote": "Since the network weights are randomly initialized, you may need to *reset* the model and restart training a few times to get decent results.",
      "section": "",
      "kind": "statement"
    }
  ]
